    "blocks": [
      {
        "id": "p1",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Every time I finish planning a holiday, I start worrying about my plants. Who will water them while I’m away? I don’t know my neighbours well enough to ask them to care for them. It’s no surprise, then, that I was "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "keenly",
            "ref": "v-keenly"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " interested when I "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "spotted",
            "ref": "v-spot"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " a self-watering plant pot at last year’s Chelsea Flower Show. Could this be the “plant sitter” I’d been dreaming of? Luckily, a two-week holiday was just around the corner—the perfect chance to test it out."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "POTR’s self-watering pots come with an "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "origami",
            "zh": "折纸"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " design—and it’s not just a pretty trick. Because they "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "fold",
            "ref": "v-fold"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " flat, more pots can be "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "shipped",
            "ref": "v-ship"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " at once, reducing their carbon footprint. Plus, the pots are made from "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "recycled",
            "ref": "v-recycled"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " plastic. And they can be recycled again at the end of their life cycle."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "I’ve never been great at origami. Even my paper airplanes are bad. But surprisingly, the pots were easy to make. I’d recommend scanning the QR code on the packaging to watch the "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "instructional",
            "ref": "v-instructional"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " video. It’s much clearer than the tiny on-pack "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "diagrams",
            "zh": "示意图"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p4",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "My holiday plan included two weeks away, with a short stop at home in between. That gave me a chance to check on my two test subjects—a "
          },
          {
            "t": "em",
            "v": "satin pothos"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " and a "
          },
          {
            "t": "em",
            "v": "calathea zebrina"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p5",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "When I returned after a sunny week in Tuscany, both plants looked healthy. The "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "wick",
            "zh": "吸水棉芯"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " was dry, so I gave it a good "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "soak",
            "zh": "浸泡"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". I also topped off the water at the bottom. But apart from that, I put aside my “"
          },
          {
            "t": "underline",
            "v": "helicopter plant parenting"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "” habits and left my plants alone."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p6",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "After the second week, I didn’t unpack right away. Rather, I hurried to see if my green friends were okay. The pothos looked perfect. The zebrina, however, looked a little tired. A quick drink quickly brought it back to life. To be fair, that might have been my fault: The inner "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "planter",
            "zh": "花盆"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " was too big to fit comfortably inside the POTR pot, so I forced it in. Next time, I’ll choose a larger planter so that it can sit properly inside with enough water at the base."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
